THE GO TOOLCHAIN
================

Three demos ship a verbatim copy of wasm_exec.js, the Go toolchain's JavaScript
shim, and each of them ships a .wasm with the Go runtime linked into it:

  demos/genai-interlingua/wasm_exec.js   demos/genai-interlingua/genai-interlingua.wasm
  demos/paladin/wasm_exec.js             demos/paladin/paladin.wasm
  demos/warden/wasm_exec.js              demos/warden/warden.wasm

All three copies of the shim are byte-identical. Each carries a header saying its
license "can be found in the LICENSE file" -- a file that did not exist in this
repository until this NOTICE was added. It is reproduced in full below, which is
what the license itself asks for and what that header was pointing at.

